# ALFI Swiss Partners — environment
#
# The enquiry form sends through Resend (ASP-67). These are SERVER-side values
# and must never be given a VITE_ prefix: anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined
# into the browser bundle by Vite and is public the moment the site deploys.
#
# Nothing here is needed to run the site locally. `npm run dev` serves the
# pages fine; only the form's send path needs these, and that path runs on the
# host, not in Vite.
#
# WHERE EACH HOST READS THEM FROM
#
#   Netlify (UAT)        Site configuration → Environment variables.
#                        netlify/functions/enquiry.mjs reads process.env.
#
#   Infomaniak (prod)    getenv(), or a PHP file returning these as an array,
#                        placed ONE LEVEL ABOVE the web root at
#                        ../alfi-config.php. Upload it once by FTP — the
#                        GitHub Actions deploy only replaces dist/ and never
#                        touches it. Above the root means Apache cannot serve
#                        it even if PHP stops executing.
#
# The key itself goes into those two places directly. It does not belong in
# this file, in .env, or anywhere else in the repository.

# Resend API key — Resend dashboard → API Keys. Begins "re_".
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Where enquiries are delivered.
ENQUIRY_TO=info@alfiswisspartners.com

# Who they appear to come from. Sending as @alfiswisspartners.com requires the
# domain to be verified in Resend first, with the SPF and DKIM records it
# gives you added to the domain's DNS. Until that is done, Resend only accepts
# its own onboarding sender, and only delivers to the account owner:
#
#   ENQUIRY_FROM=ALFI Swiss Partners <onboarding@resend.dev>
#
# After verification:
ENQUIRY_FROM=ALFI Swiss Partners <enquiries@alfiswisspartners.com>
